Note:   1. For Java 8 and below, use JKS, otherwise use PKCS12 as the storetype
        2. When using a self-signed certificate, we need only to export it from the Keystore file
        3. Otherwise, if we're going to work with a CA-signed certificate, then we need to create a certificate signing request (CSR file - sender_certificate.csr), then we        import; 
                1. keytool -certreq -alias senderKeyPair -storetype PKCS12 \
                  -keystore sender_keystore.p12 -file -rfc \
                  -storepass changeit > sender_certificate.csr

                2. Loading a Public Key for Verification
                    keytool -importcert -alias senderKeyPair -storetype PKCS12 -keystore 
